.TH LUNE 1 "2026" "Lune" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lune \- GPU-accelerated Wayland terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lune
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.br
.B lune msg
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fIACTION\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lune
is a modern, GPU-accelerated Wayland terminal emulator for Linux featuring
Classic and Modern layouts, tabs and split panes, command blocks and bookmarks,
Kitty graphics protocol support, scrollback search, Vi mode, Quick Select hints,
built-in themes, and live configuration reloading.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-working\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Start the initial shell or command in \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-title " " \fITITLE\fR
Set the initial window title.
.TP
.BR \-\-class ", " \-\-app\-id " " \fIID\fR
Set the Wayland application ID (default: \fBlune\fR).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Load configuration from \fIPATH\fR instead of the default configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-command " " \fICMD\fR " [" \fIARGS\fR ...]
Run \fICMD\fR with optional \fIARGS\fR instead of the default shell.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS lune msg
Send a command to a running Lune window over its local Unix socket. When
\fB\-\-socket\fR is omitted, \fBlune msg\fR uses \fBLUNE_IPC_SOCKET\fR if set
or selects the most recently active local socket.
.TP
.BR "new-tab" " [" \-d " " \fIDIR\fR "] [" \-T " " \fITITLE\fR "] [" \-e " " \fICMD\fR " ...]"
Open a new tab in the target window.
.TP
.BR "split" " [" \-\-right | \-\-down | right | down "] [" \-d " " \fIDIR\fR "]"
Split the focused pane (default: \fBright\fR).
.TP
.BR "set-theme" " " \fINAME\fR
Switch the active color theme at runtime. Accepts \fBsystem\fR, \fBdark\fR,
\fBlight\fR, any built-in preset (\fBcatppuccin-mocha\fR, \fBcatppuccin-latte\fR,
\fBtokyo-night\fR, \fBtokyo-night-day\fR, \fBgruvbox-dark\fR,
\fBgruvbox-light\fR, \fBnord\fR, \fBdracula\fR, \fBrose-pine\fR,
\fBrose-pine-dawn\fR, \fBkanagawa\fR, \fBone-dark\fR), or a custom theme name.
.TP
.B reload-config
Force-reload configuration from disk.
.TP
.B save-config
Save current runtime settings into the active configuration file.
.TP
.B list
Print active Lune IPC socket paths.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Lune reads \fI${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/lune/lune.conf\fR and reloads
automatically when saved. Custom color themes can be placed in
\fI${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/lune/themes/<name>.conf\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for user configuration (default: \fI~/.config\fR).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory used for per-user IPC sockets (\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lune/\fR) and
temporary shell integration scripts.
.TP
.B LUNE_IPC_SOCKET
Exported automatically to shells launched by Lune, pointing to the current
window's IPC socket.
.TP
.B SHELL
Default interactive shell launched when \fBshell\fR is not configured.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/lune/lune.conf
User configuration file.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/lune/themes/
User custom color themes.
